  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the diagram, it follows that $m∠A={180}^{∘}>{0}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement II is true, and statement III is false. Indeed, from the graph we deduce  that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B+{100}^{∘}+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+m∠C & ={80}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of each of the angles $∠B$ and $∠C$ is less than ${80}^{∘},$ so these angles are acute angles.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
